--
--
N5008 [temp.arg.template]/1: the template-argument for a template
template-parameter is a template-name, which may be a QUALIFIED id
(`user<outer::box>`).  CBMC's TT-argument typecheck only accepts a
single unqualified name: "found no match for symbol 'outer'" followed
by "expected template name for template template parameter".
Found round 122 while writing cpp11_tt_param_base_in_namespace (kb3
had to move its driver inside the namespace to dodge this).  Accepted
by g++ and clang++ -std=c++11 -fsyntax-only.  Header-free, minimal.
Likely fix site: the TT-argument path in typecheck_template_args /
resolve (the same family as the 5face51cef id_map fix, but on the
ARGUMENT side rather than the parameter-use side).
